Error: Jet.FieldWriteWithoutMarker: `.remove()` changes `world`, which has read access only
  --> Tests/UI/pool_changes_need_a_writable_pool.jet:9:5
    |
  9 |     world.remove(id).drop("only the refusal matters here")
    |     ^^^^^
 Why: `remove: fn(^self, id: ID<Player>)` changes the value it's called on, but an unmarked parameter gives read access only
 Fix: Change the parameter to `world: ^Slots<Player>`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.FieldWriteWithoutMarker

Error: Jet.FieldWriteWithoutMarker: `.add()` changes `world`, which has read access only
  --> Tests/UI/pool_changes_need_a_writable_pool.jet:12:51
    |
 12 | recruit: fn(world: Slots<Player>) -> ID<Player> { world.add(Player{name: "Ash"}) }
    |                                                   ^^^^^
 Why: `add: fn(^self, value: ^^Player)` changes the value it's called on, but an unmarked parameter gives read access only
 Fix: Change the parameter to `world: ^Slots<Player>`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.FieldWriteWithoutMarker

Error: Jet.FieldWriteWithoutMarker: Cannot write to `world` — it has read access only
  --> Tests/UI/pool_changes_need_a_writable_pool.jet:14:57
    |
 14 | rename: fn(world: Slots<Player>, id: ID<Player>) { world[id] = Player{name: "Rem"} }
    |                                                         ^^^^
 Why: An unmarked parameter gives read access only; assigning into it needs write access
 Fix: Change the parameter to `world: ^Slots<Player>`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.FieldWriteWithoutMarker
